NAME

ulibBit - Returns the value of a bit in a bit field


SYNOPSIS

UBYTE ulibBit(UBYTE *StartByte, long Position)
                     a0              d0


DESCRIPTION

This function returns the value of bit number <Position> of the memory array
pointed to by <StartByte>.

Note that in this case bitfields run in a rather strange manner, since
<StartByte> is an unbounded array (an array of unknown length).  Example:

MemLoc    7  6  5  4  3  2  1  0
MemLoc+1  7  6  5  4  3  2  1  0

Result = ulibBit(MemLoc, 0);  /* Gets value of bit MemLoc   "0" */
Result = ulibBit(MemLoc, 1);  /* Gets value of bit MemLoc   "1" */
Result = ulibBit(MemLoc, 8);  /* Gets value of bit MemLoc+1 "0" */
Result = ulibBit(MemLoc, 12); /* Gets value of bit MemLoc+1 "4" */


NOTES

This function is used internally by Xenolink, and will not be useful to
application developers.  This function will most likely be discontinued in
version 2.0 of Xenolink.


RETURNS

0 if the bit is not set.
1 if the bit is set.


SEE ALSO

ulibSetBit
